            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0495" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.94/856: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-27T09:00:00+03:00">October 27, 1935—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 27—4:53 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>463. My telegram No. 459, October 25, 1 p.m. Dr. Yen, Chinese Ambassador, last
                    night informed me in the utmost confidence that <pb facs="0496" n="384"
                        xml:id="pg384"/> he had just received a most secret communication from China
                    saying that the Japanese Government was bringing pressure of most urgent nature
                    on the Chinese Government with a view to obtaining support of the Chinese
                    Government for an attack on the Soviet Union.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
